    {
      "t": "html",
      "html": "<div class=\"notes\"><b>Hinweise:</b> Both argc and argv are mutable in the function. This is done to allow injection and interpretation of vendor specific ARA configuration information. The injected arguments are removed in accordance with <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CORE_15006\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf)\">[SWS_CORE_15006]</a>. Error scenarios, such as corrupted configuration files, are expected to be handled in an implementation-defined way - either as a Non-Standardized Violation (<a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CORE_00003\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf)\">[SWS_CORE_00003]</a>) or as a vendor-specific error code (<a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CORE_00092\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf)\">[SWS_CORE_00092]</a>).</div>",
